Usage:
  concord --help
  concord --version
  concord zl <work> -- <prompt>   # start or resume a session
  concord zl <work> --project <project>   # land in that member Project of the work
  concord zl --resume-last   # resume the last workspace
  concord session    # internal TTY bootstrap; session identity env required
  concord continuity-block <directory>   # read-only continuity packet for the session directory
  concord host-lease < JSON stdin      # record this host session's release lease (adapter-invoked)
  concord host-leases                  # print live release leases; prunes stale ones
  concord upgrade < JSON stdin      # apply pending migrations; {"plan":true} reports readiness
  concord repair < JSON stdin          # verify assets, back up the database, repair the installed release (#912)
  concord recover-fold-guard < JSON stdin   # offline: clear a stranded fold guard and rebuild projections from the log
  concord ci-wait < JSON stdin         # one bounded slice of a GitHub CI wait (CD-0160)

Required-field refusals exit 64 before dispatch.
Commands read one strict JSON object from stdin:
  concord invoke < JSON stdin
    required: call_envelope{schema_version, request_id, client_ref, principal_ref, session_ref, agent_ref, directory, worktree, ambient_project_id, scope_version, manifest_digest}, tool, operation, input
    optional: call_envelope.selected_product_id, call_envelope.host_assertion_digest, call_envelope.host_approval_assertion; pre-dispatch decode refusals exit 64; worktree_verify input uses command OR oracle (phase prepare | execute), never both; worktree_inspect mode oracle_output uses run_ref, stream stdout | stderr, offset, length (1-16384 raw bytes), never path or idempotency_key; exact fields and exclusions follow the generated agent contracts
    accepted values: tool.operation: concord_product_view.resolve | concord_product_view.snapshot | concord_product_view.portfolio | concord_product_view.blocked_sessions | concord_product_view.resources | concord_work_browse.list | concord_work_browse.blocked | concord_work_browse.ready | concord_work_browse.scope | concord_work_browse.resource_claims | concord_work_browse.messages | concord_work_browse.worktree_audit | concord_work_browse.worktree_inspect | concord_work_trace.history | concord_work_trace.observations | concord_work_trace.external_observations | concord_work_trace.relations | concord_work_trace.continuity | concord_work_trace.research | concord_work_trace.project_retirement | concord_knowledge.search | concord_knowledge.resolve_note | concord_knowledge.unprocessed | concord_work_define.capture | concord_work_define.revise_intent | concord_work_define.research_pack_create | concord_work_define.research_revision_append | concord_work_define.research_finding_record | concord_work_define.research_source_record | concord_work_define.research_freshness_set | concord_work_define.research_retire | concord_work_define.observation_record | concord_work_define.issue_link_record | concord_work_transition.lifecycle | concord_work_transition.remove | concord_work_transition.workflow_action | concord_work_transition.worker_reconcile | concord_work_transition.worker_abandon | concord_work_transition.worktree_claim | concord_work_transition.session_vacate | concord_work_transition.project_handoff_record | concord_work_transition.project_handoff_consume | concord_work_transition.worktree_reclaim | concord_work_transition.worktree_audit_reclaim | concord_work_transition.worktree_verify | concord_work_transition.worktree_destroy | concord_work_relate.set_memberships | concord_work_relate.link | concord_work_relate.unlink | concord_work_relate.supersede | concord_work_relate.restore_superseded | concord_work_relate.resolve_overlap | concord_work_relate.resource_claim | concord_work_relate.resource_release | concord_work_relate.message_send | concord_work_relate.message_withdraw | concord_work_compact.publish | concord_work_compact.reconcile | concord_work_compact.lesson_publish | concord_domain.list | concord_domain.detail | concord_domain.active_work | concord_domain.attachments | concord_domain.overlaps | concord_domain.observation_record | concord_domain.observation_dismiss | concord_work_transition.correct_delivery | concord_work_relate.product_project_add | concord_work_relate.client_policy_grant_request | concord_work_transition.outside_repair | concord_work_transition.outside_repair_reconcile
  concord worker-dispatch < JSON stdin
    required: event_id, work_id, attempt_id, lane_id, lane_version, lane_digest, packet_schema_version, report_schema_version, packet_digest
    optional: readback_model (host-reported executing model); terminal ('failed') with terminal_failure_kind and terminal_detail for an attempt born failed, such as a lost or ambiguous readback; host_provenance.digest (sha256), host_provenance.sources[] (kind: agent_definition | agents_md | instruction_file | unenumerated; path; sha256) — required for v3 evidence (CD-0034); worker_job (job_id, revision, digest) — required on a job-bound attempt (CD-0205)
  concord worker-complete < JSON stdin
    required: event_id, work_id, attempt_id, readback_model, report_schema_version, evidence_origin
    optional: worker_directory, base_comparison, review, worker_job — required on a job-bound attempt, evidence[] — required when evidence_origin is reported, context_findings[] (0-16 typed claims, 16 KiB)
    accepted values: evidence_origin: reported | legacy_unavailable; evidence[].obligation: bounded_findings | commands | contract_findings | exit_codes | failure_classification | files_touched | severity | source_citations | uncertainties | unresolved_issues | verification_commands | visual_artifacts; reported evidence must discharge every declared obligation; base_comparison.checks[]: pass | fail | not_run; review: ship | no_ship, findings severity P0-P3, confidence low | medium | high; ship refuses P0, no_ship refuses zero findings; a lane requiring the typed review block refuses a completion without it and a free-text severity entry beside it; the block discharges severity; context_findings[].kind: observation | inference | hypothesis | rejected_approach | open_question | contradiction | direction
  concord worker-fail < JSON stdin
    required: event_id, work_id, attempt_id, readback_model, failure_kind, detail
    optional: context_findings[] (as worker-complete; worker_error only)
    accepted values: failure_kind: fallback_blocked | worker_error | invalid_report | abandoned
  concord worker-abandon < JSON stdin
    required: event_id, work_id, attempt_id, detail
    accepted values: the host signs a worker-fail assertion with failure_kind abandoned; readback_model is derived from the dispatched attempt
  concord client-register < JSON stdin
  concord client register < JSON stdin
    required: client_ref, key_id, principal_ref, public_key, capabilities, product_scope, project_scope, agent_scope
    accepted values: capabilities: product_read | work_define | work_transition | work_relate | work_compact | cross_scope | research | worker_evidence | worker_dispatch; public_key: base64 Ed25519; agent_scope: the agent references this client may present
  concord client-policy-update < JSON stdin
  concord client policy-update < JSON stdin
    required: client_ref, principal_ref, capabilities, product_scope, project_scope, agent_scope
    accepted values: capabilities: product_read | work_define | work_transition | work_relate | work_compact | cross_scope | research | worker_evidence | worker_dispatch; agent_scope: the agent references this client may present
  concord client-policy-expand < JSON stdin
  concord client policy-expand < JSON stdin
    required: client_ref
    optional: capabilities, product_scope, project_scope, agent_scope — additive union; every existing grant and the stored principal are preserved (CD-0097 D6)
    accepted values: capabilities: product_read | work_define | work_transition | work_relate | work_compact | cross_scope | research | worker_evidence | worker_dispatch
  concord client-key-rotate < JSON stdin
  concord client key-rotate < JSON stdin
    required: client_ref, key_id, public_key
    accepted values: public_key: base64 Ed25519
  concord client-revoke < JSON stdin
  concord client revoke < JSON stdin
    required: client_ref
  concord product-create < JSON stdin
  concord product create < JSON stdin
    required: product_id, display_name, stage_maturity, stage_audience_commitment, project_id, project_display_name, role
    optional: reason
    accepted values: stage_maturity: prototype | alpha | beta | production | deprecated; stage_audience_commitment: operator_only | limited | public; role: primary | secondary
  concord resource-create < JSON stdin
  concord resource create < JSON stdin
    required: event_id, resource_id, product_id, display_name, class, kind, purpose, stage_maturity, stage_audience_commitment, environments, expected_product_version
    optional: locator_absence_reason, metadata_schema_version, metadata, owner_purpose, owner_environments
    accepted values: stage_maturity: prototype | alpha | beta | production | deprecated; stage_audience_commitment: operator_only | limited | public
  concord resource-share < JSON stdin
  concord resource share < JSON stdin
    required: event_id, resource_id, product_id, expected_resource_version
    optional: purpose, environments
  concord domain-project-attachments-replace < JSON stdin
  concord domain project-attachments-replace < JSON stdin
    required: event_id, product_id, domain_id, expected_version, attachments
    optional: attachments (replaces the full edge set)
    accepted values: attachments[].role: primary | secondary
  concord domain-resource-attachments-replace < JSON stdin
  concord domain resource-attachments-replace < JSON stdin
    required: event_id, product_id, domain_id, expected_version, attachments
    optional: attachments (replaces the full edge set)
  concord project-create < JSON stdin
  concord project create < JSON stdin
    required: project_id, display_name, product_id, role, expected_product_version
    optional: reason
    accepted values: role: primary | secondary
  concord product-project-add < JSON stdin
  concord product project-add < JSON stdin
    required: product_id, project_id, role, expected_version
    optional: reason
    accepted values: role: primary | secondary
  concord product-stage-update < JSON stdin
  concord product stage-update < JSON stdin
    required: product_id, stage_maturity, stage_audience_commitment, expected_version
    optional: reason (cite the CD-0091 rung manifest when raising maturity)
    accepted values: stage_maturity: prototype | alpha | beta | production | deprecated; stage_audience_commitment: operator_only | limited | public
  concord product-knowledge-home-designate < JSON stdin
  concord product knowledge-home-designate < JSON stdin
    required: product_id, project_id, locator_id, expected_version
    optional: reason
    accepted values: locator_id: a canonical_path locator of the member Project
  concord product-knowledge-home-clear < JSON stdin
  concord product knowledge-home-clear < JSON stdin
    required: product_id, expected_version
    optional: reason
  concord product-knowledge-source-register < JSON stdin
  concord product knowledge-source-register < JSON stdin
    required: product_id, project_id, locator_id, expected_version
    optional: reason
    accepted values: locator_id: a canonical_path locator of the member Project, not the designated home
  concord product-knowledge-source-remove < JSON stdin
  concord product knowledge-source-remove < JSON stdin
    required: product_id, project_id, locator_id, expected_version
    optional: reason
    accepted values: locator_id: a registered knowledge source of the Product
  concord project-locator-add < JSON stdin
  concord project locator-add < JSON stdin
    required: project_id, locator_id, kind, value, expected_version
    accepted values: kind: canonical_path | git_remote
  concord project-locator-update < JSON stdin
  concord project locator-update < JSON stdin
    required: project_id, locator_id, kind, value, expected_version
    accepted values: kind: canonical_path | git_remote
  concord project-locator-remove < JSON stdin
  concord project locator-remove < JSON stdin
    required: project_id, locator_id, expected_version
  concord project-canonical-path < JSON stdin
  concord project canonical-path < JSON stdin
    required: project_id
  concord cd-reservations < JSON stdin
  concord cd reservations < JSON stdin
    required: directory
    accepted values: prints the law-addition reservations (law_id, owner_work_id) of the Product that owns the calling checkout, with checkout_work_id naming the work that owns the checkout; read-only
  concord backup < JSON stdin
    required: destination
    accepted values: destination: absolute clean path that does not yet exist; a manifest is written beside it
  concord worktree-locate < JSON stdin
    required: project_id, work_id
    optional: ref (a rev-syntax ref; defaults to HEAD, the default branch under the trunk-stays-on-default rule)
  concord claim-landing < JSON stdin
    required: work_id, session_ref, landed_directory
  concord vacate-landing < JSON stdin
    required: work_id, session_ref, landed_directory
  concord work-bootstrap < JSON stdin
    required: product_id, project_id, title, value_statement, kind, task, idempotency_key
    optional: priority, urgency, tags, workflow_type_ref, external_ref, governing_requirements, ref (default branch resolved after identity), defect_intake (required for bug), host_pid (required with session_ref); handler refusals exit 2; required-field refusals exit 64
    accepted values: kind: task | bug | decision | research | other; urgency: standard | expedite
  concord work-resume < JSON stdin
    required: product_id, project_id, work_id
    optional: handler refusals exit 2; required-field refusals exit 64
  concord receipt < JSON stdin
    required: work_id
    accepted values: prints the product-owned closure receipt markdown (CD-0169) for a completed work item; empty output when the item is not completed
  concord work-shelve < JSON stdin
    required: operation_id, idempotency_key, work_id, expected_version, handoff
    optional: product_id, linear, actor, safety evidence
    accepted values: reason is fixed to shelved; no sixth lifecycle state
  concord work-cancel < JSON stdin
    required: operation_id, idempotency_key, work_id, expected_version, handoff
    optional: product_id, linear, actor, safety evidence
    accepted values: reason is fixed to cancelled; removal is not archival
  concord ci-wait < JSON stdin
    required: selector, repo
    optional: mode (pr checks|merge), time_seconds_max, state_file
    accepted values: selector.kind: pr|sha|run; mode: checks|merge
  concord session-prepare < JSON stdin
    required: product_id, work_id, agent
    optional: task (max 8192 bytes; none on resume); agent is the active agent; handler refusals exit 2; required-field refusals exit 64
  concord outside-repair < JSON stdin
    required: work_id, agent
    optional: none; requires an active outside-repair hold and a controlling TTY; JSON stdout names the exact directory and argv; host I/O uses /dev/tty
  concord project-resolve < JSON stdin
  concord project resolve < JSON stdin
    required: directory
    optional: worktree (defaults to directory)
  concord restore < JSON stdin
    required: source, destination
    accepted values: source: existing verified backup snapshot path; destination: absolute clean path that does not yet exist and is not the live database
  concord predecessor-inventory < JSON stdin
  concord predecessor inventory < JSON stdin
    required: snapshot_path
    accepted values: snapshot_path: absolute path to a predecessor snapshot file (CD-0097)
  concord predecessor-import < JSON stdin
  concord predecessor import < JSON stdin
    required: snapshot_path, product{product_id, display_name, stage_maturity, stage_audience_commitment}, projects, select_change_ids
    optional: dry_run, surfaces
    accepted values: stage_maturity: prototype | alpha | beta | production | deprecated; stage_audience_commitment: operator_only | limited | public; projects[].role: primary | secondary; select_change_ids: change ids the snapshot enumerates as active and that belong to a declared snapshot_project_id, or already-imported ids that turned terminal or left the active set since the previous harvest; surfaces: specifications | active_work | terminal_history | wisdom | reflections; only active_work imports, a surface outside this set refuses before import (CD-0097)
  concord host-lease < JSON stdin
    required: pid
    optional: directory, worktree: session location, named by a breaking-migration refusal; advisory, never interpreted
    accepted values: pid: the host process that holds this release; the core writes the lease under the data root
  concord host-leases < JSON stdin
    required: 
    accepted values: prints the live host leases and prunes stale ones (CD-0111 D2)
  concord upgrade < JSON stdin
    required: 
    optional: plan: read-only readiness report; confirm_sessions_stopped: no session runs on an unfenceable release tree
    accepted values: applies pending migrations; a breaking step runs only inside the maintenance boundary, which excludes session admission until activation and refuses under a live older session (CD-0111 D3)
